==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~16.67 seconds<sup>30f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 26.67~36.67 seconds<sup>800f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The One Horn leaves you with no real way to rush this stage, so prepare like any normal [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] fight and get a couple of [[Worker Cat]] levels before the enemies get close to your base. You'll have to worry about the One Horn more than the Zombies in this stage, but be wary of of their burrowing. As always, [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cats]] are recommended to be used in moderation so you can clean up your backline.

A strong [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] (such as [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]]) will do you very well, just like in the normal stage. Just keep up the pressure with proper meatshielding just like most One Horn fights and you'll be just fine. Zomboe does pose a bit of a threat, but it's very slow and doesn't burrow too far, so dispatching it shouldn't be too tough, just be aware that it outranges UFO Cat and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]].

